// A fact is filed under the body that wrote it, whatever the build's paths and whatever stack addresses its
// buffers land at. The emitter files an allocation by its position in a buffer, and named the buffer by its
// ADDRESS: a fact recorded against a scratch buffer that is never resolved (the header's instance of
// `Optional<string>`'s destructor, here) was matched by a later module's buffer at the same stack address, and
// its position read against that text. Before `0.9.945` this program was refused, *"a deep `copy` of `string` …
// `f…` is `@noheap`"*, naming whichever body spanned the offset; a program whose `@noheap` render path was its
// own was refused under some spellings of its manifest's path and not others, since `#line` carries the path.
// Sixty-four `@noheap` bodies fill this module so that any misfiled offset lands in one. Returns 67.
import { core::println };

@noheap fn int32 f0(int32 x) {
    int32 a = x * 1; int32 b = a + 0; int32 c = b - x; int32 d = c * 2;
    if (d > 1000) { return d - a; } if (c > 500) { return c + b; } return a + b + c + d - 0;
}
